Switch: the deko3d NRO's device and present (AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D)

docs/DEKO3D_MIGRATION_PLAN.md phase 2. With AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D (switch/native/CMakeLists.txt,
COS_SWITCH_RENDERER=deko3d) Aurora keeps recording and encoding every frame, against Dawn's Null
device (no GPU work, nothing drawn: the GX encoding is a no-op in this phase), and switch/deko owns
the GPU through the C functions of switch/deko/dk_aurora.h:
- webgpu::initialize: the Null backend, no WebGPU surface, the GL NRO's feature set (the Null device
  offers every feature: CoreFeaturesAndLimits is left out so the pipeline configs match the GL
  NRO's), then aurora_switch_dk_init (device, queue, memory, swapchain, DKSH cache); the frame
  buffers are created without a surface; shutdown calls aurora_switch_dk_shutdown;
- aurora.cpp: no SDL renderer for the Null backend, no surface checks in begin_frame; end_frame
  submits the Null device's command buffer, then imgui::present_deko3d presents (timed as the
  present in the perf-switch lines) instead of the surface acquire, the blit and the ImGui pass;
- imgui.cpp: no imgui_impl_wgpu; the font atlas and aurora_imgui_add_texture go to
  aurora_switch_dk_imgui_texture, the frozen draw data to aurora_switch_dk_present.
Without AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D (the GL NRO, the Mac) nothing changes.

Switch only (switch/native/aurora/patches); not for upstream.

